<title>BRAZIL: Bolivia-Brazil gas pipeline contract awarded.</title>
<headline>Bolivia-Brazil gas pipeline contract awarded.</headline>
<dateline>RIO DE JANEIRO 1997-01-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>A Brazilian/Japanese consortium has been awarded a $665 million contract to supply the steel tubes for the entire stretch of the 1,900-mile (3,000-km) Bolivia-Brazil gas pipeline, a company official said.</p>
<p>The consortium formed by Brazilian tube manufacturer Confab and Japanese trading company Marubeni Corp will supply a total of 540 tonnes of steel tubes for the pipeline, a Confab spokeswoman said.</p>
<p>The $1.8 billion gas pipeline which will link Bolivia's natural gas fields with the industrial heartland of Brazil is due to come online in late 1998.</p>
<p>((--Simona de Logu, Rio de Janeiro newsroom, 5521 507 4151))</p>
